cdp:st:C2a:
\begin{proposition}[Euler localization for torus fibrations]\label{cdp:st:C2a}
\StatementRecord{cdp:st:C2a}{proved}{Historical records: GPT-6 Astra (OpenAI, ChatGPT Pro mode), effort Pro, 17 November 2026; Claude Fable 5.2 (Anthropic), effort high, 16 November 2026. Also checked in this writing by \CurrentChecker. The finite critical-value set, proper submersion trivializations over the complement, compact-support Euler additivity and the top Chern/Euler comparison give the stated sum over reduced supports. Scheme multiplicities leave the underlying topological support unchanged}{the hypotheses, notation and definitions stated here; the explicit constructions and calculations in the proof}

Let $g:Y\to C$ be a proper surjective holomorphic map from a connected compact complex manifold to a compact Riemann surface, with connected general fibre $F$. Let $\Sigma\subset C$ contain every critical value. Then $\Sigma$ can be chosen finite, and
\[
 e(Y)=e(C\setminus\Sigma)e(F)+\sum_{c\in\Sigma}e((Y_c)_{\rm red}). \tag{C.1}\label{cdp:eq:C.1}
\]
For a complex threefold with general fibre a complex two-torus this becomes
$\int_Yc_3(T_Y)=e(Y)=\sum_{c\in\Sigma}e((Y_c)_{\rm red})$.
\end{proposition}
